#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/tab-completion.md:2
msgid "Tab completion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/tab-completion.md:4
msgid ""
"Starting with snapd 2.30, commands and aliases packaged in snaps are able to "
"perform tab-completion in the bash shell, and in the future that same "
"mechanism may be enabled in other shells as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/tab-completion.md:6
msgid ""
"For this to work, a `completer` key must be specified under the application "
"scope in snap.yaml or snapcraft.yaml, pointing to a bash completion snippet "
"(that would in traditional packaging be dropped in `/usr/share/bash-"
"completion/completions`). With that, `snapd` will create the necessary "
"system setup to run the completer script confined. The completer must be for "
"the full app name (`<snap>.<app>`), without considering aliases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/tab-completion.md:8
msgid ""
"Two sample snaps that implement this are the `http` and `test-snapd-"
"complexion` (edge) snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/tab-completion.md:10
msgid ""
"Snapcraft has had support for the `completer` attribute of snap apps since "
"version 2.33."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/tab-completion.md:12
msgid ""
"Debugging tab completion of a strict snap can be hard, so we [wrote a guide "
"for it](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/debugging-tab-completion/4198)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/tab-completion.md:14
msgid ""
"Extending this tab completion mechanism to other shells (zsh for example) is "
"relatively simple. All that is needed is a marshaller of the completion "
"request. See [`complete.sh` in the snapd source](https://github.com/"
"canonical/snapd/blob/master/data/completion/bash/complete.sh) for details."
msgstr ""
